$NetBSD$

Install the binaries and the man pages under the name
program_transform_name asks for, so that more than one Emacs can share
a prefix.  21.4 accepts --program-transform-name and never uses it.

No ${DESTDIR} here: the package passes prefix=${DESTDIR}${PREFIX} and
mandir=${DESTDIR}... in INSTALL_MAKE_FLAGS, so bindir and man1dir
already carry it and adding it again writes .destdir twice.

--- Makefile.in.orig
+++ Makefile.in
@@ -77,6 +77,11 @@
 ### like `18.59' or `19.0'.
 version=@version@
 
+# Program name transformation.
+TRANSFORM = @program_transform_name@
+EMACS_NAME = `echo emacs | sed '$(TRANSFORM)'`
+EMACSFULL = `echo emacs-${version} | sed '$(TRANSFORM)'`
+
 ### This should be the name of the configuration we're building Emacs
 ### for, like `mips-dec-ultrix' or `sparc-sun-sunos'.
 configuration=@configuration@
